   "name": "The creek Gračnica",
   "subtitle": "",
   "description": "The district is salmonid and spreads through the canyon of the creek Gračnica which is extremely rich in wild brown trouts. Even the counts of Celje had fished here centuries ago. The creek Gračnica can be listed among better preserved waters in eastern Slovenia. Its journey begins on 460 m altitude and runs in approximately 20km long channel to the outflow into the Savinja near Rimske toplice."
